WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.436
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.904
We hope you're all
doing well tonight.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:05.905
And now, if you don't mind,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.106
I'm going to get to the news.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.341
During his remarks at
Saturday's White House

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:11.244
correspondents' dinner,
President Biden said,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.613
"American democracy
is not a reality show."

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:15.648
And he's right.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.384
Reality shows get
much better ratings.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.552
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.420
According to a new poll,
President Biden's

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.656
approval rating has increased
slightly

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.992
over the last two months,
and now the White House

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:29.195
is scrambling like hell
to figure out what he did.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.864
"Did he change his hair?
A different mask?

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.633
What tie was he wearing?"

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.801
That's right, President Biden's
approval rating

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.570
has increased to 42%.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.640
He now ranks slightly above
leaf blowers.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.608
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.577
At his rally in Nebraska
yesterday,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:48.181
former president Trump appeared
to misremember Ohio Republican

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.550
Senate candidate
J.D. Vance's name

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.585
and called him J.D. Mandel.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.021
That's bad enough, but then he
said, "J.D. Mandel will win

00:00:56.021 --> 00:00:58.324
or my name isn't Donald Vance."

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.460
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.896
According to a new poll, just
35% of college students said

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.400
they like Elon Musk more than
other megabillionaires.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.770
Said Musk, "Oh, yeah?
How much to buy college?"

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.338
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.908
"Not just yours.
The whole idea."

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.810
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.347
After the share price of Meta
increased by over 17% last week,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:26.419
CEO Mark Zuckerberg became $11
billion wealthier in one day.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:29.589
Then that became $12 billion
when he stuck his hand

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.125
in the pocket of a hoodie
he hadn't worn in a while.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.525
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:36.162
"Ooh, that's fortuitous."

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.064
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:41.267
A couple recently got married on
a Southwest flight to Las Vegas

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.203
and then immediately started
watching different movies.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:48.140
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.976
It deserved better.
That's a wonderful joke.

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:53.779
I didn't think it would go well.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.381
But it was too good not to do.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.216
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:00.786
A lot of you aren't married yet,
but you're going to be,

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:03.155
and then one day you're going to
be lying in bed

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.458
and you're going to realize how
[bleep] funny that joke was.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.827
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.061
I'm willing -- You know what?

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.763
I'm willing to make
that investment now.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.764
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.499
Equity. That joke has equity.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.636
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.037
That's right.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:21.006
A couple recently got married on
a Southwest flight to Las Vegas,

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.908
and like most couples
who go to Vegas,

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:24.978
decided to get divorced
on the flight back.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.213
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.982
According to a new survey,
more than half of Americans want

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.217
their family to have access
to their personal phone

00:02:32.217 --> 00:02:34.220
and computer data
after they die.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.555
The other half are men.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:39.124
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:42.695
And finally, a single lottery
ticket was sold in Arizona

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:47.232
last week that won the
$473 million Powerball jackpot,

00:02:47.232 --> 00:02:48.701
and the big winner was --

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.136
Aw, damn it!

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.938
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.774
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

